      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The majority holds that the remaining parents plausibly allege a present, concrete impairment of their authority to participate in their minor child's care from Washington's parental-exclusion scheme, rather than merely self-imposed precautions against a future runaway episode, so the absence of an imminently expected shelter visit does not defeat injury in fact at the pleading stage."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The majority confines its standing ruling to parents with a gender-dysphoric minor child and particularized allegations of impaired parental participation; it does not adopt the United States' categorical rule giving every objecting parent standing whenever a law changes parental control over medical care, regardless of the family's circumstances."
    }
  ],
